<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 15 February, from 1113 to 1965.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1113 CE <span class="tih-ago">913 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Paschal II recognises the Knights Hospitaller</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The bull Pie postulatio voluntatis placed the hospital of St John in Jerusalem under papal protection. The order later took on a military role and survives today as the Sovereign Military Order of Malta.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1564 CE <span class="tih-ago">462 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo Galilei is born in Pisa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Galileo's telescopic discoveries, including Jupiter's moons, and his studies of motion made him a founder of modern physics. His defence of Copernicus brought his trial by the Inquisition in 1633.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1898 CE <span class="tih-ago">128 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">USS Maine explodes in Havana harbour</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An explosion sank the American battleship, killing some 260 men. The cause is still debated, but US newspapers blamed Spain, and the cry 'Remember the Maine' helped bring war in April.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/singapore" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/singapore.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1942 CE <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Singapore surrenders to Japan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General Arthur Percival surrendered Singapore, and some 80,000 British, Indian and Australian troops became prisoners. Churchill called it the worst disaster and largest capitulation in British history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1961 CE <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US figure skating team killed in the Sabena air crash</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sabena Flight 548 crashed on approach to Brussels, killing all 72 aboard and a man on the ground. Among the dead was the entire US figure skating team, en route to the world championships in Prague.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1965 CE <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Canada raises its Maple Leaf flag</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The red and white Maple Leaf flag was raised on Parliament Hill in Ottawa, replacing the Canadian Red Ensign. 15 February is now marked as National Flag of Canada Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li></ol>
